Id: stor019i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
Fix: Give /home and /var file systems of their own (partition, LVM volume or btrfs subvolume), mounted nodev,nosuid.
References: fstab(5); CIS Distribution Independent Linux Benchmark 1.1.2 (Configure Filesystems, level 2)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

/home or /var is a directory on the root file system rather than a
file system of its own. It then shares the root's space, so a user
filling their home, or a service filling /var, fills / and the system
stops; and it shares the root's mount options, so nodev and nosuid
(stor017w) cannot be set for it alone. The CIS Benchmark asks for
separate partitions at its level 2; most stock installs (Debian,
Ubuntu, Arch, Alpine) have one root file system, Fedora Workstation
makes /home a btrfs subvolume, so this is a layout choice to make at
install time rather than a weakness, and it stays informational.

Separating them later means a new partition or LVM volume (or a btrfs
subvolume), the data copied across, and an fstab line with
nodev,nosuid; disk quotas are the other way to keep one user from
filling the disk.
